{"tool_name":"giniclust2","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"giniclust2","home":"https://github.com/dtsoucas/GiniClust2","license":"MIT","summary":"Clustering algorithm for the simultaneous detection of common and rare cell types from single-cell gene expression data.","addition_date":"2018-08-16T07:36:20Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-25T14:28:52.361680Z","tool_type":["Library"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:giniclust2","credit":[{"email":"dtsoucas@g.harvard.edu","name":"Daphne Tsoucas","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["User manual"],"url":"https://github.com/dtsoucas/GiniClust2/blob/master/Reference_manual.pdf"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Expression profile clustering","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0313"}]}],"name":"GiniClust2","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"d.gabrielaitis","publication":[{"doi":"10.1186/s13059-018-1431-3","metadata":{"abstract":"Single-cell analysis is a powerful tool for dissecting the cellular composition within a tissue or organ. However, it remains difficult to detect rare and common cell types at the same time. Here, we present a new computational method, GiniClust2, to overcome this challenge. GiniClust2 combines the strengths of two complementary approaches, using the Gini index and Fano factor, respectively, through a cluster-aware, weighted ensemble clustering technique. GiniClust2 successfully identifies both common and rare cell types in diverse datasets, outperforming existing methods. GiniClust2 is scalable to large datasets.","authors":[{"name":"Tsoucas D."},{"name":"Yuan G.-C."}],"citationCount":52,"date":"2018-05-10T00:00:00Z","journal":"Genome Biology","title":"GiniClust2: A cluster-aware, weighted ensemble clustering method for cell-type detection"},"pmcid":"PMC5946416","pmid":"29747686"}],"topic":[{"term":"Cell biology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_2229